course: dictionary
lesson: 15632
title: A tendency is a likely habit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tendency is what someone or something often does, or is likely to do. «He has a tendency to forget his PE kit.» This does not mean he forgets it every single day. It means forgetting is something he does often, so it is likely to happen again.
explain: Tendency can also mean the direction something is moving in. «There is a tendency for the days to get colder in November.» Here you are not talking about one cold day. You are talking about the way the weather is heading.
explain: Look at the words around tendency to find its meaning. Words like «often», «likely» and «to forget» are clues. If you can swap in «a habit» or «a trend» and the sentence still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: Tendency is a noun. Its plural is tendencies.
fact: «A tendency to» means you often do something or are likely to do it.
fact: «Tendency» can also mean a general direction in which something is changing; this is called a trend.
fact: «Central tendency» is a maths word: it is the middle or typical value of a set of data, found by the mean, median or mode.
fact: «Metals have a tendency to rust» means metals are likely to rust, especially when they are wet or damp.
exercise: «He has a tendency to forget his PE kit.» What does tendency mean here? | A rule set by the teacher | A loud shout at lunchtime | A kit bag for PE | *A habit of often doing something
exercise: «Sales have a tendency to fall in the winter.» What does tendency show about sales? | *The direction they are usually moving in | They are always exactly the same | They have been stolen | They are sold at a shop
exercise: «The mean, median and mode are all measures of central tendency.» What is central tendency in maths? | A mistake made in a sum | The biggest number in a list | A kind of graph with bars | *The middle or typical value of a set of data
test: «Metals have a tendency to rust.» What does this sentence tell you? | Metals are likely to rust | Metals are shiny and smooth | *Metals often rust, or are likely to rust | Metals never rust
test: Ella says, «Tom has a tendency to be late on Mondays.» What does tendency mean? | *Tom is often late, or is likely to be late | Tom likes Mondays best | Tom is always early | Tom has a new bike
exam: Which sentence uses tendency to mean a likely habit? | The tendency of the dog was to bark | Please tendency the plants today | The tendency is in the cupboard | *Ruby has a tendency to talk in class when she is excited
